\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\loch\af31506\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \loch\af43\dbch\af31505\hich\f43 \u-10178\'3f\u-8736\'3f}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  SLIDE 4 \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Background: Key Concepts
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 This slide has two parts \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  left (LLMs) and right (LIME vs SHAP).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Left side \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  How LLMs work (explain simply):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
"Large Language Models are deep neural networks trained on billions of words from the internet. They use a mechanism called self-attention to understand context across long sentences."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "When generating text, they work token by token \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 one word at a time. At each step, the model looks at all previous words and predicts what comes next based on probability. There is a setting called 'temperature' \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  if temperature is high, the model is mor
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 e creative and random; if low, it is more predictable."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Key insight to emphasize:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "Human writing has irregularities \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 rhythm changes, unusual word choices, personal style. LLM-generated text tends to be very grammatically regular and lexically predictable. These differences are measurable \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  and that's what detection systems exploit."}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Right side \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  LIME vs SHAP (this is technical, explain carefully):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 LIME \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Local Interpretable Model-Agnostic Explanations:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
"LIME works by asking: what happens if I hide different words in this text? It systematically masks words, observes how the AI detector's decision changes, and builds a simple explanation: 'these 3 words most strongly pushed the model to say this is AI-ge
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 nerated.' It is fast but can give slightly different answers each time because of randomness."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 SHAP \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  SHapley Additive Explanations:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
"SHAP comes from cooperative game theory. Imagine each word in the text is a 'player' in a game, and the final prediction is the 'prize.' SHAP calculates exactly how much each word contributed to the final prediction \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 fairly, considering all possible com\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 binations. It is more consistent than LIME but takes more computing power."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Both methods:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "Both LIME and SHAP are post-hoc \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 meaning they explain decisions AFTER the model has made them. Both are local \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  they explain one specific text at a time, not the whole model. And both are model-agnostic \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 they work with any type of AI model."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Three paradigms at the bottom:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
"Detection research falls into three approaches: classical stylometric methods, transformer-based deep learning, and multi-label attribution. We will examine each one."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
