\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16654193 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\loch\af31506\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \loch\af43\dbch\af31505\hich\f43 \u-10179\'3f\u-8221\'3f}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  SLIDE 6 \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Theme 1: Stylometric & Classical ML
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Introduction:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "The first cluster of studies uses the oldest and most interpretable approach \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 stylometry. Stylometry means measuring writing style through handcrafted features. These are features a human expert could also inspect."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Study 1 \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Shah et al. (2023):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "Shah and colleagues trained three classical classifiers \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  SVM, Logistic Regression, and Random Forest 
\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  on stylometric features like syllable counts, punctuation ratios, and lexical diversity. They applied both LIME and SHAP to explain the results."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "What did they find? Simpson's Index \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  a measure of vocabulary diversity \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 and punctuation regularity were the two strongest indicators of AI authorship. Both LIME and SHAP agreed on this finding despite using completely different mechanisms. That agreeme\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 nt is significant."}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
"Limitation: Their dataset only covered general English text. We don't know if these features work in specialized domains like medical or legal writing."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Study 2 \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  McGovern et al. (2024):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "McGovern's team asked a different question: not just 'is this AI?' but 'which AI wrote it?' They analyzed POS \hich\f31506 \emdash 
\loch\f31506  Part of Speech \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  distributions across GPT-3.5, GPT-4, Llama, and other models."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "They found that each LLM has a stylistic fingerprint \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 a characteristic pattern of how often it uses adjectives, nouns, passive constructions. They did not use LIME or SHAP formally, but their finding is conceptually important: LLMs write differently fro\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
m humans AND from each other."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Study 3 \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Przystalski et al. (2025):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "The most technically rigorous of the three. They tested whether stylometry works on SHORT texts \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 under 200 words. Think Twitter posts, student short answers, peer review comments."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "Using SHAP, they found that grammatical standardization was the single most powerful feature \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 carrying twice the weight of the next most important feature. Human writing, even in short texts, has grammatical irregularities \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  sentence fragments, delibera\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
te rule-breaking. LLMs follow grammar so perfectly that the consistency itself becomes suspicious."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Bottom banner:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "The shared finding across all three studies: LLM text is more grammatically regular and lexically predictable than human text."}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
