\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid16654193 \rtlch\fcs1 \af31507\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 
\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\loch\af31506\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af37 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f37\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \loch\af37\dbch\af31505\hich\f37 \u-10178\'3f\u-8587\'3f}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  SLIDE 7 \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Theme 2: Transformers + The Adversarial Paradox
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Introduction:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "The second cluster uses transformer-based deep learning \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 much more powerful than classical methods, but also much harder to interpret."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Study 1 \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Mitrovic et al. (2023):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "Mitrovic's team fine-tuned DistilBERT \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  a lightweight version of the famous BERT model \hich\f31506 \emdash 
\loch\f31506  specifically to detect short ChatGPT-generated product reviews. They achieved around 84% accuracy."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "SHAP analysis revealed something interesting: ChatGPT reviews consistently overuse words like 'exceptional,' 'outstanding,' 'perfect' 
\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  evaluative superlatives. Human reviews use idiosyncratic, personal language and hedged evaluations like 'it's pretty g\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
ood, but...' These patterns are now auditable, not just a black-box verdict."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Study 2 \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Joshi et al. (2024) \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  HULLMI:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "HULLMI is the most important single study in this review. It compared everything \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 Naive Bayes, Random Forest, and multiple transformer models \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  on a multi-source dataset with texts from several different LLMs."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
"The winner was RoBERTa-Sentinel with about 91% accuracy. More importantly, they proved that adding LIME explanations did NOT reduce accuracy. This directly challenges the common assumption that 'more powerful = less interpretable.' You can have both."}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 "LIME revealed that the model was detecting formulaic hedging language, impersonal constructions, and overly smooth transitions \hich\f31506 
\emdash \loch\f31506  not random noise. The explanations made sense linguistically."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Study 3 \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Masih et al. (2025):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
"Masih's team did the most comprehensive comparison of LIME vs. SHAP applied to transformers. Their most practically important finding: sometimes the model is correct for the wrong reasons \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
 it detects AI text because of topic-specific vocabulary, not tru\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 e stylistic markers. XAI makes this visible so you can fix it."}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af43 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f43\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \loch\af43\dbch\af31505\hich\f43 \u9888\'3f\loch\af43\dbch\af31505\hich\f43 \u-497\'3f}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  The Adversarial Paradox \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  Mohammadi et al. (2025):}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Speak slowly and emphasize this \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  it's the most provocative finding in the entire review.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
"Now here is where it gets really concerning. Mohammadi and colleagues asked: if LIME and SHAP tell us exactly which words triggered the AI detection \hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506  what happens if we simply replace those words with synonyms?"}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid16654193\charrsid16654193 
